{"key":"permutations-7d862e677b40138c","sourceHash":"7d862e677b40138c5278c48633400a525b66fefc17696771532df485ee133e07","pattern":"permutations","category":"backtracking","title":"Challenge: Permutation Backtracking","idea":"Choose one unused item for the next position, recurse, then mark it unused again.","complexity":"O(n*n!) time · O(n) state excluding output","source":"fn permutation_count(values: &[i32]) -> usize {\n    fn choose(used: &mut [bool], depth: usize) -> usize {\n        if depth == used.len() {\n            return 1;\n        }\n        let mut total = 0;\n        for i in 0..used.len() {\n            if !used[i] {\n                used[i] = true;\n                total += choose(used, depth + 1);\n                used[i] = false;\n            }\n        }\n        total\n    }\n    choose(&mut vec![false; values.len()], 0)\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let result = permutation_count(&[1, 2, 3]).to_string();\n    println!(\"{result}\");\n}\n","sites":[{"line":16,"function":"permutation_count","statement":"choose(&mut vec![false; values.len()], 0)"},{"line":3,"function":"choose","statement":"if depth == used.len() {"},{"line":4,"function":"choose","statement":"return 1;"},{"line":6,"function":"choose","statement":"let mut total = 0;"},{"line":7,"function":"choose","statement":"for i in 0..used.len() {"},{"line":8,"function":"choose","statement":"if !used[i] {"},{"line":9,"function":"choose","statement":"used[i] = true;"},{"line":10,"function":"choose","statement":"total += choose(used, depth + 1);"},{"line":11,"function":"choose","statement":"used[i] = false;"},{"line":12,"function":"choose","statement":"}"},{"line":14,"function":"choose","statement":"total"},{"line":20,"function":"main","statement":"let result = permutation_count(&[1, 2, 3]).to_string();"},{"line":21,"function":"main","statement":"println!(\"{result}\");"},{"line":22,"function":"main","statement":"}"}],"version":1,"input":"[1,2,3]","stdout":"6\n","values":[{"type":"&[i32]","data":{"kind":"l